{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","level":2,"text":"The four rules","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"computed property \/ expression","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body. Origami ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier — that’s a different concept).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","level":3,"text":"Pure value patch → computed property","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","level":3,"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","level":3,"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings"},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"title":"Drag","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","abstract":[{"text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","title":"Beats","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"title":"Interaction","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic"}}}